    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Education",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S5718\n\nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act directing the state department of education to develop a\ncomprehensive plan for increasing access to and lending of electronic\nbooks in public libraries and public library systems across New York\nstate\n\nPURPOSE:\n\nTo develop a plan that will help increase the public's access to\nelectronic books through their local libraries.\n\nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nThis legislation would direct the Commissioner of the State Education\nDepartment to conduct a study and develop a comprehensive plan for\nincreasing access to and lending of electronic books in libraries and\nlibrary systems across New York State. The bill lists several issues\nthat shall be reviewed as part of the study. The study and plan shall\nbe submitted by June 1, 2016.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nMore recently, the demand for electronic books has increased\nsignificantly. As the shift from print books to electronic books has\noccurred, library patrons have been increasingly eager to access\nelectronic books in formats that are compatible with popular digital\ndevices. The publishing industry uses a series of business models that\nenable certain forms of e-lending in libraries. However, the library\nand library systems have found that these business models offer\nelectronic books at higher costs and contain many restrictions on\naccess to and use of the electronic books. The purpose of this\nlegislation is to study how electronic books are currently being sold\nand distributed to libraries and library systems in New York State.\nThis legislation also directs the Commissioner of the State Education\nDepartment to develop a comprehensive plan for increasing access to\nand lending of electronic books in libraries and library systems.\n\nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2014, Referred to the Senate Education Committee; Passed Assembly\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nMinimal.\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nImmediate.\n\n",
